<p>So far, I&rsquo;m enjoying <a href="https://taonaw.com/2026/04/19/testing-inkwell-by-microblog.html">Inkwell</a>. The main advantages over my FreshRSS setup is mainly the speed and the cleaner UI.</p>
<p>Since I discover most of my RSS feed via blogs and reading posts online, I already have the browser open, and adding a new feed to Inkwell is faster then doing so on FreshRSS because my Synology needs to wake up if it&rsquo;s hibernating, then it needs to log me in - and sometimes the container FreshRSS is on is not available for some reason and I need to restart it or wait patiently. Not an issue with Inkwell.</p>
<p>There are a few issues that need to be polished out, especially on the web and the Mac version, but I&rsquo;m already leaning into the philosophy behind the app: read what&rsquo;s new today, and don&rsquo;t worry about what I missed. It&rsquo;s easy enough to visit the Inkwell blog and read past posts if needed.</p>
